# Architecture Lifecycle

Every agent session MUST follow this protocol for architecture files.

## At session start (before coding)

1. Read `PROJECT-STRUCTURE.md` — folder ownership and responsibilities.
2. Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` — current system design, integrations, and recent changes.
3. Read `PRODUCT.md` when the task touches product scope, brand, or launch constraints.
4. Skim `docs/` for any surface-specific doc relevant to the task (e.g. `docs/seo-route-matrix.md`, `docs/surfaces/blog.md`).

## During work

- Stay within your agent scope (see `agent-delegation.mdc`).
- If you discover a structural change (new route, new module, new integration, moved folder), note it for the session-end update.

## At session end (before finishing)

Update `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` when your work changed any of:

- Routes or locale pairs (`src/lib/i18n/routes.ts`)
- API endpoints or auth flows
- Blog provider, Sanity wiring, or admin surfaces
- Deployment / env vars / third-party integrations
- Module boundaries or folder ownership

Add a dated entry under **Recent changes** with: what changed, which paths were touched, and any follow-up needed.

If folder ownership or agent scopes changed, update `PROJECT-STRUCTURE.md` as well.

Do not leave architecture docs stale after meaningful code changes.
